<% content_for :title, "A record-backed editor · yrby" %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <script type="module" src="<%= busted "/document.js" %>"></script>
<% end %>
<div class="docs-body max-w-3xl">
  <p class="text-sm text-accent">Example</p>
  <h1>A record-backed editor</h1>
  <p>Open this page in two windows and type in either one. Rails saves the
    document to its database, and the button below reads it back in Ruby.</p>
  <p>Everyone who visits this page edits the same document, and it's cleared
    after a day with no activity. Don't type anything private.</p>
</div>
<p id="document-status" role="status" class="my-4 text-sm text-zinc-400">Connecting…</p>
<template id="document-template">
<%= collaborative_document_tag @document, :body, id: "document-editor", class: "block rounded-lg border border-zinc-700 bg-zinc-900 p-3" do %>
  <div data-editor-mount aria-label="Shared document"></div>
<% end %>
</template>
<div id="document-container"></div>
<section class="docs-body mt-8 max-w-3xl">
  <h2>Read back from Rails</h2>
  <button id="read-document" class="rounded border border-zinc-600 px-3 py-2 text-sm">Read saved text</button>
  <pre id="stored-document" aria-live="polite">Type something, then select “Read saved text”.</pre>
  <%= code_block "ruby", "doc = @document.collaborative_document(:body).y_doc\ndoc.read_text(\"content\")" %>
  <h2>How it's wired</h2>
  <p>The view renders <code>collaborative_document_tag</code>. When the
    document syncs, the page's script attaches CodeMirror to it, and it
    destroys the editor when the lease's abort signal fires. Edits that
    haven't been acknowledged are held by the document session, so removing
    the editor doesn't lose them.</p>
  <p>This page runs the published gems and client. The site adds its
    public-demo limits to the shipped channel. In your own app, check that the
    user can edit the record before you render the tag.</p>
  <p><a href="/docs/getting-started">Getting started</a> ·
    <a href="/docs/javascript-client">The JavaScript client</a></p>
</section>
